{"id":"c719484a-7f42-43c5-ba9a-0e3930203be5","object":"chat.completion","created":1789996876,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"schema\": \"amr-supervisor/v1\",\n  \"select\": [\n    {\n      \"when\": \"OwnerFree and RequestA\",\n      \"action\": \"SelectA\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"OwnerFree and RequestB\",\n      \"action\": \"SelectB\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"True\",\n      \"action\": \"Defer\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"step\": [\n    {\n      \"when\": \"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted\",\n      \"action\": \"Brake\",\n      \"next\": \"Stopped\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and not Halted\",\n      \"action\": \"Brake\",\n      \"next\": \"BrakeRequested\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"AtGoal and Released and not Halted\",\n      \"action\": \"Brake\",\n      \"next\": \"BrakeRequested\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"AtGoal and Released and Halted\",\n      \"action\": \"Finish\",\n      \"next\": \"Done\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ\",\n      \"action\": \"Release\",\n      \"next\": \"Traversing\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted\",\n      \"action\": \"Brake\",\n      \"next\": \"BrakeRequested\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"not OwnReservation and not Released\",\n      \"action\": \"Request\",\n      \"next\": \"Waiting\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"ModeStopped\",\n      \"action\": \"Resume\",\n      \"next\": \"ResumePending\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"when\": \"True\",\n      \"action\": \"Proceed\",\n      \"next\": \"Traversing\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","reasoning_content":"We need answer only JSON. Need synthesize supervisor rules for select and step. Need parse policy carefully. Need produce exactly JSON object keys schema, select, step. Need no markdown.\n\nWe need design select function and step function satisfying policy. Need at most 12 rules each. Need expressions allowed. Need all possible inputs result. Need explicit next mode for step. Need evaluate all combinations. Need model correspondence.\n\nWe need infer policy. Need produce ordered rules.\n\nSelect: inputs OwnerFree, RequestA, RequestB, PreferA, PreferB. Actions SelectA, SelectB, Defer.\n\nRequirements:\n- Selecting A requires OwnerFree and RequestA.\n- Selecting B requires OwnerFree and RequestB.\n- If OwnerFree and at least one request exists, select an eligible robot, rather than Defer. Otherwise Defer.\n- When both eligible, either is legal; preferences advisory not obligation, may conflict or absent.\n\nSo simple:\n1 when OwnerFree and RequestA and not RequestB -> SelectA? But if both, can choose either. Need ensure if OwnerFree and RequestA true, select A unless maybe prefer B? Since both legal either. Could just prioritize A when RequestA, regardless RequestB:\n1 when OwnerFree and RequestA -> SelectA\n2 when OwnerFree and RequestB -> SelectB\n3 True -> Defer\nCheck if OwnerFree true RequestA false RequestB true -> SelectB. If OwnerFree true RequestA true RequestB false -> SelectA. If both -> SelectA. If OwnerFree false any -> Defer because first false second false. If OwnerFree true no requests -> Defer. This satisfies. Preferences ignored. Conditions length fine. Need exactly maybe 3 rules. Could use Prefer? not needed. \"Preferences do not impose additional acceptance obligation.\" We can ignore. OK.\n\nStep: more complex. Need modes. Inputs ObservationUsable, PedestrianBlocked, OwnReservation, Released, BodyClearOfZ, Halted, AtGoal, TaskActive. Mode flags ModeIdle etc exactly one.\n\nActions Request, Proceed, Brake, Resume, Release, Finish. Next mode one of Idle, Waiting, Traversing, BrakeRequested, Stopped, ResumePending, Done. No terminal shortcut, all modes.\n\nPolicy P2 exceptions to normal operation. Need synthesize priority.\n\nLet's restate.\n\nOrdinary step outcome is Proceed, entering Traversing. Displaced by following requirements. Authority highest to lowest:\n1 invalid/blocked/task-inactive handling\n2 released-goal handling\n3 whole-body release\n4 unfinished braking\n5 reservation request\n6 restart transition\n7 ordinary motion\n\nNeed map.\n\nHighest: whenever ObservationUsable is false, TaskActive is false, or PedestrianBlocked true, return Brake. Under that highest-priority condition, enter Stopped if Halted true and BrakeRequested otherwise. Thus even arrived halted robot must obey highest if blocked/invalid.\nSo rule H1: when not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked -> action Brake, next = if Halted then Stopped else BrakeRequested. Since expression and next cannot be conditional? Step rule has action fixed string and next fixed mode. Need split into two rules:\n- if invalid/blocked/task-inactive and Halted -> Brake, next Stopped.\n- if invalid/blocked/task-inactive and not Halted -> Brake, next BrakeRequested.\nThese have same priority, order doesn't matter (mutually exclusive Halted). Need ensure first.\n\nNext: released-goal handling higher than all below. Arrival with AtGoal and Released both true: without Halted, return Brake and enter BrakeRequested; with Halted, return Finish and enter Done.\nSo rules:\n- AtGoal and Released and not Halted -> Brake, BrakeRequested.\n- AtGoal and Released and Halted -> Finish, Done.\nThis is after highest. Note if invalid/blocked/task-inactive also true, highest overrides. So order these after H1/H2.\n\nNext: whole-body release: OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release, entering Traversing, before unfinished braking is considered.\nSo rule:\n- OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ -> Release, Traversing.\nNeed consider maybe Released? Policy says OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ. This authority after released-goal. If AtGoal Released etc higher? Yes released-goal higher. If highest invalid, higher. So place after.\n\nNext: unfinished braking: BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested; overrides missing-reservation request. This is about current mode? \"BrakeRequested without Halted\" maybe means current mode BrakeRequested and Halted false? Or input? Let's parse: \"unfinished braking; BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested; this overrides a missing-reservation request.\" Since step expression can refer to mode flags. Current mode exactly one. \"BrakeRequested without Halted\" likely ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted. It says BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested. So rule:\n- ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted -> Brake, BrakeRequested.\nWhat if ModeBrakeRequested and Halted? Then unfinished braking not apply; perhaps could proceed? Need other requirements. We'll handle.\n\nNext: reservation request: A missing reservation requires Request, entering Waiting, when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true; this overrides restart transition.\nSo rule:\n- not OwnReservation and not Released -> Request, Waiting.\nBut wait \"missing reservation\" maybe if task active? But all facts. Policy says \"when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true\". This authority lower than unfinished braking, so if ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted then Brake even if missing reservation. Also lower than whole-body release? If OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ, release before request (but missing reservation can't be true if OwnReservation true). Lower than released-goal. Highest invalid still.\n\nNext: restart transition: applies to current Stopped mode and yields Resume, entering ResumePending. A missing reservation requires Request... overrides restart transition. So rule:\n- ModeStopped -> Resume, ResumePending.\nBut only after reservation request. However if missing reservation (neither OwnReservation nor Released) then Request first. If ModeStopped and missing reservation -> Request Waiting. If ModeStopped and has reservation/released -> Resume. Also if other higher conditions apply.\n\nNext: ordinary motion: Proceed entering Traversing. Default for remaining cases.\n\nNeed ensure all modes/combinations covered. Need consider all policy descriptions and priorities. Need decide exact expression order and conditions.\n\nImportant: \"The ordinary step outcome is Proceed, entering Traversing. It is displaced by the following requirements. Their authority, from highest to lowest is...\" This implies default Proceed Traversing for all not matched. But some higher requirements may apply regardless of mode and facts. Need cover every combination.\n\nNeed be careful about \"BrakeRequested without Halted\" might refer to current action? Actually mode BrakeRequested. It says \"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested\". Since modes include BrakeRequested, yes current mode. It does not mention if current mode is not BrakeRequested but Halted false. Only current mode.\n\n\"restart transition applies to a current Stopped mode and yields Resume, entering ResumePending.\" So only ModeStopped.\n\nNeed not infer relationships. We evaluate all 7*256 combinations, so some weird: ModeDone with AtGoal Released Halted -> Finish Done even though already Done. ModeDone with missing reservation -> Request Waiting? According to authority, if no higher, missing reservation requires Request entering Waiting. Since applies every mode. So yes even Done if no reservation and not released. But if Done mode and TaskActive true, ObservationUsable true, PedestrianBlocked false, AtGoal? Maybe AtGoal false, Released true? Need parse.\n\nWe need build ordered rules that implement priorities globally. Need account for all conditions from each policy. Let's define inputs and modes.\n\nModes: Idle, Waiting, Traversing, BrakeRequested, Stopped, ResumePending, Done. Exactly one mode flag true.\n\nPolicy hierarchy:\nP0 highest: INVALID = not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked.\nAction Brake. Next = Stopped if Halted else BrakeRequested.\n\nP1 released-goal: AtGoal and Released.\n- if not Halted -> Brake BrakeRequested.\n- if Halted -> Finish Done.\nBut if P0 applies, P0 wins. So P1 rules after P0.\n\nP2 whole-body release: OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ -> Release Traversing. Applies if P0/P1 not. Note Released? If AtGoal and Released and Halted P1 wins; if AtGoal Released not Halted P1 wins. If no AtGoal/Released, release.\n\nP3 unfinished braking: ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted -> Brake BrakeRequested. Applies if P0/P1/P2 not. Note P2 could apply if OwnReservation BodyClear true; but if ModeBrakeRequested and BodyClear true, P2 has higher authority than unfinished braking. So whole-body release wins over unfinished braking. Policy says \"However, OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release, entering Traversing, before unfinished braking is considered.\" Yes. So P2 before P3. Thus if ModeBrakeRequested, Halted false, but OwnReservation+BodyClearOfZ true, action Release Traversing, not Brake. Is that intended? Let's parse: \"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested; this overrides a missing-reservation request. However, OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release, entering Traversing, before unfinished braking is considered.\" Yes, whole-body release before unfinished braking. So yes.\n\nP4 missing reservation: not OwnReservation and not Released -> Request Waiting. Applies if not P0-P3. Note if ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted, P3 wins. If ModeStopped and missing, P4 wins over restart.\n\nP5 restart: ModeStopped -> Resume ResumePending. Applies if not P0-P4. But note if ModeStopped and missing reservation, P4 wins. If ModeStopped and OwnReservation or Released but not P2/P3? P2 if OwnReservation+BodyClear, P3 if ModeBrakeRequested not relevant. So P5.\n\nP6 ordinary: Proceed Traversing.\n\nNeed encode.\n\nPotential issue: P4 \"missing reservation requires Request, entering Waiting, when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true\". This is unconditional on mode, task active, etc. But if invalid etc, P0 wins. If AtGoal Released true, then Released true, P4 false. If AtGoal Released false but OwnReservation false, P4 true, so even if AtGoal true? P1 requires Released true. If AtGoal true, Released false, no P1. P4 may Request Waiting rather than maybe something else. Is that expected? The policy says missing reservation requires Request when neither OwnReservation nor Released true. It applies. So yes.\n\nWhat about P2 OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ. If OwnReservation true, P4 false. P2 applies regardless of mode. So if ModeDone and OwnReservation+BodyClear, action Release Traversing. Is that intended? \"These rules apply to every input combination and mode; no special terminal-mode shortcut.\" yes.\n\nNeed ensure \"AtGoal and Released both true: without Halted, return Brake and enter BrakeRequested; with Halted, return Finish and enter Done.\" This P1 applies even if OwnReservation+BodyClear. Yes released-goal higher than whole-body release. So if AtGoal Released Halted and OwnReservation BodyClear, P1 Finish Done. If AtGoal Released not Halted, P1 Brake. If AtGoal Released Halted and invalid, P0 Brake Stopped. Good.\n\nNeed maybe handle \"invalid/blocked/task-inactive handling\" with Halted true: enter Stopped. If Halted false: enter BrakeRequested. Action Brake. If already ModeStopped and Halted true? Action Brake next Stopped. Fine.\n\nNow need create JSON arrays. Need expressions allowed. We can use names and mode flags. Use Python precedence: not, and, or. Parentheses allowed. Need no comparisons. Need no calls. True/False allowed. Need exactly one rule per condition/action/next. At most 12 rules. Let's count step rules:\n\n1 P0 Halted: (not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted -> Brake, Stopped\n2 P0 not Halted: (not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and not Halted -> Brake, BrakeRequested\n3 P1 not Halted: AtGoal and Released and not Halted -> Brake, BrakeRequested\n4 P1 Halted: AtGoal and Released and Halted -> Finish, Done\n5 P2: OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ -> Release, Traversing\n6 P3: ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted -> Brake, BrakeRequested\n7 P4: not OwnReservation and not Released -> Request, Waiting\n8 P5: ModeStopped -> Resume, ResumePending\n9 P6: True -> Proceed, Traversing\n\nThat's 9 rules. Need ensure P0 rules before P1. P1 not Halted and P0 Halted? P0 Halted condition includes Halted, P1 not Halted excludes Halted, so no conflict. P1 Halted and P0 Halted? P0 Halted wins because placed before. Good. P1 Halted and P0 not Halted impossible because Halted both? P0 not Halted excludes Halted. So fine.\n\nNeed check P2 before P3. Yes. P3 before P4. Yes. P4 before P5. Yes. P5 before P6.\n\nBut need consider P0 rules: if invalid and Halted true, next Stopped. If invalid and Halted false, next BrakeRequested. What if invalid and Halted true but action Brake and next Stopped. Yes.\n\nPotential subtlety: P0 \"whenever ObservationUsable is false, TaskActive is false, or PedestrianBlocked is true, return Brake. Under that highest-priority condition, enter Stopped if Halted is true and BrakeRequested otherwise.\" So action Brake always. We split by Halted. Good.\n\nPotential subtlety: \"without Halted\" in P1 might mean Halted false. Yes.\n\nPotential subtlety: \"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake\" Could \"BrakeRequested\" refer to action? But actions don't include BrakeRequested. It must refer to mode. We use ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted. If current mode BrakeRequested and Halted true, P3 not apply. Then what? If no other, P4/P5/P6. For ModeBrakeRequested Halted true, if missing reservation (not OwnReservation and not Released) then P4 Request Waiting. If OwnReservation+BodyClear then P2 Release. If Released and AtGoal true then P1. Else ordinary Proceed Traversing. Is that correct? Policy says BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake. With Halted, braking finished, so normal. Could proceed if clear. OK.\n\nPotential subtlety: \"Whole-body release: OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release, entering Traversing, before unfinished braking is considered.\" It doesn't mention Released or AtGoal. We do.\n\nPotential subtlety: \"reservation request; A missing reservation requires Request, entering Waiting, when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true; this overrides restart transition.\" It says \"missing reservation\" maybe only if not OwnReservation and not Released. Yes.\n\nPotential subtlety: \"released-goal handling; Higher than all these is arrival with AtGoal and Released both true...\" Actually wording: \"Higher than all these is arrival...\" Wait let's re-read policy text:\n\n\"Policy presentation P2: exceptions to normal operation.\n\nThe ordinary step outcome is Proceed, entering Traversing. It is displaced by the following requirements. Their authority, from highest to lowest, is: invalid/blocked/task-inactive handling; released-goal handling; whole-body release; unfinished braking; reservation request; restart transition; ordinary motion.\n\nThe restart transition applies to a current Stopped mode and yields Resume, entering ResumePending. A missing reservation requires Request, entering Waiting, when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true; this overrides the restart transition. BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested; this overrides a missing-reservation request. However, OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release, entering Traversing, before unfinished braking is considered.\n\nHigher than all these is arrival with AtGoal and Released both true: without Halted, return Brake and enter BrakeRequested; with Halted, return Finish and enter Done. Highest of all, whenever ObservationUsable is false, TaskActive is false, or PedestrianBlocked is true, return Brake. Under that highest-priority condition, enter Stopped if Halted is true and BrakeRequested otherwise. Thus even an arrived and halted robot must obey this highest-priority rule if its input is blocked or invalid.\"\n\nSo hierarchy as above. Good.\n\nNeed maybe include select rules. Select at most 12. We'll use 3.\n\nNeed final JSON exactly. Ensure valid JSON. No extra fields. Root keys exactly schema, select, step. Schema value \"amr-supervisor/v1\". select array of objects with when/action. step array with when/action/next.\n\nNeed ensure no duplicate JSON keys. We'll not.\n\nNeed ensure expressions use only allowed names. We use:\nselect: OwnerFree, RequestA, RequestB. OK.\nstep: ObservationUsable, TaskActive, PedestrianBlocked, Halted, AtGoal, Released, OwnReservation, BodyClearOfZ, ModeBrakeRequested, ModeStopped. OK. No select names. No mode names with Mode prefix? Step can refer to ModeIdle etc. We use ModeBrakeRequested, ModeStopped. OK.\n\nNeed consider condition length and nodes. Simple.\n\nNeed maybe include parentheses around or in P0. Expression: \"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted\". Python precedence: not has higher than and, or lower than and? Actually Python precedence: not > and > or. So \"not A or not B or C and Halted\" would parse as (not A) or (not B) or (C and Halted), not what we want. We need parentheses. Our expression with parentheses is fine. Nodes? small.\n\nP0 not Halted: \"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and not Halted\". Note \"not Halted\" okay. Precedence: and has higher than or, but parentheses done. The \"not Halted\" is fine.\n\nP1: \"AtGoal and Released and not Halted\". Python precedence: not > and, so AtGoal and Released and (not Halted). OK. Could parenthesize but not needed.\nP2: \"OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ\". OK.\nP3: \"ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted\". OK.\nP4: \"not OwnReservation and not Released\". Python precedence: not > and, so (not OwnReservation) and (not Released). OK.\nP5: \"ModeStopped\". OK.\nP6: \"True\". OK.\n\nNeed think about totality: For any step input, first matching rule. If highest invalid not matched, P1 etc. Eventually True -> Proceed. All covered. But is True allowed? Yes expressions allow True, False. Good.\n\nPotential issue: At most 32 total branches. We have 3 + 9 = 12. Fine. At most 12 per function. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"A step rule also requires 'next' (mode string).\" We include next for all step rules. Select rules no next.\n\nPotential issue: \"select cannot use any step or mode names; step cannot use any select names.\" We comply.\n\nNow, but we should not be too hasty. Need consider if select rules should consider preferences? The policy says \"When both robots are eligible, either is legal; preferences do not impose an additional acceptance obligation, and their values may conflict or both be absent.\" So ignoring prefer is legal. But maybe there is a hidden requirement: \"If a reservation is free and at least one request exists, select an eligible robot, rather than Defer.\" Our select rules: if OwnerFree and RequestA -> SelectA even if RequestB also. If OwnerFree and RequestA false RequestB true -> SelectB. If OwnerFree true RequestA false RequestB false -> Defer. If OwnerFree false RequestA true RequestB false -> first false (OwnerFree false), second false (OwnerFree false), third Defer. Good.\n\nWhat if OwnerFree true RequestA true RequestB true, PreferB true. We select A. Is that allowed? Yes either is legal, preferences advisory. Good.\n\nNow step deeper. Let's examine all mode/fact combinations to see if rules exactly implement authority. Could there be a need to handle \"ObservationUsable false, TaskActive false, or PedestrianBlocked true\" even if Halted? We do. Under that condition, if Halted true -> Stopped; else BrakeRequested. Good.\n\nCould there be a conflict between P1 and P0? P0 higher. We place P0 first. For invalid and AtGoal Released Halted true: P0 Halted rule action Brake next Stopped. This matches \"even an arrived and halted robot must obey highest-priority rule if blocked/invalid.\" Yes.\n\nWhat about invalid and AtGoal Released Halted false: P0 not Halted action Brake next BrakeRequested. P1 also same action Brake next BrakeRequested. No issue.\n\nWhat about P1 Halted vs P0? If invalid and AtGoal Released Halted true, P0 wins Brake Stopped, not Finish Done. We place P0 before P1. Good.\n\nWhat about P2 vs P3: We place P2 before P3. If ModeBrakeRequested, not Halted, OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ true, P2 Release Traversing. Policy says whole-body release before unfinished braking. Good.\n\nWhat about P2 vs P4: OwnReservation true so P4 false. No conflict.\n\nWhat about P2 vs P5: ModeStopped, OwnReservation+BodyClear -> P2 Release Traversing, not Resume. Is that intended? Hierarchy says whole-body release higher than unfinished braking, reservation request, restart. So yes, if in Stopped and OwnReservation+BodyClear, release before restart. But is that physically plausible? Could be. Policy applies all combinations. Good.\n\nWhat about P3 vs P4: ModeBrakeRequested, not Halted, not OwnReservation, not Released -> P3 Brake, not Request. Policy says unfinished braking overrides missing-reservation request. Good.\n\nWhat about P3 vs P5: ModeBrakeRequested not Halted cannot be ModeStopped because exactly one mode. So no conflict.\n\nWhat about P4 vs P5: ModeStopped, not OwnReservation, not Released -> P4 Request Waiting, not Resume. Policy says missing reservation overrides restart. Good.\n\nWhat about P5 vs P6: ModeStopped, OwnReservation or Released, not P2/P3/P4 -> Resume ResumePending. If ModeStopped and Released true but AtGoal false, P4 false because Released true. P5 Resume. Is that correct? \"restart transition applies to a current Stopped mode and yields Resume, entering ResumePending.\" It doesn't require reservation. Missing reservation overrides. If Released true, no missing reservation, so